From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Nguyen <tienthong2004@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 10:25:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/15] imsservice: Report the real IMS registration state

The AOSP-compat hooks in ImsMmtelFeature.addRegistrationListener and
GoogleImsService.setRegistrationListener told Android IMS was registered
on LTE as soon as it attached, on every slot, even without a SIM. A call
placed before the real registration (e.g. right after a SIM is
inserted) then went to IMS, which refused it, and hung at "calling".

Keep the capability report, drop the forced registration from
addRegistrationListener, and in setRegistrationListener report
registered only if the phone has a VoLTE registration, as open() does.
Real registration events reach Android as before.

Assisted-by: LLM
